{"id": "20260715174913311765_b05cd784", "type": "Claim", "text": "Earlier in the twentieth century, some scholars, particularly in 
the 1920s, regarded the Ring of Nestor and comparable Cretan‑Mycenaean gold rings such as the Ring of Minos as forgeries, largely 
because of their obscure or legendary find circumstances, but this tendency has been reassessed in favor of their authenticity in 
recent research.", "source_ids": ["20260715174845023769_648c270f"], "citations": [17], "sources": [{"source_id": 
"20260715174845023769_648c270f", "title": "(2020) A. G. Vlachopoulos, “The Ring of Nestor and the quest for authenticity”, in F. 
