t_Approaches_and_New_Perspectives_in_Aegean_Iconography_Aegis_18_2020_pp_223_252", "source_type": "paper", "published_at": null}]}, 
{"id": "20260715174913377930_edeef646", "type": "Claim", "text": "In the ring’s iconography, the key figure that Arthur Evans had 
described as a ‘watch‑dog’ or ‘dragon’ guarding an old ‘tree of the world’ is reinterpreted by a recent study as a scorpion, which 
is proposed to be a major apotropaic (protective) symbol in Bronze Age Aegean imagery.", "source_ids": 
["20260715174845023769_648c270f"], "citations": [17], "sources": [{"source_id": "20260715174845023769_648c270f", "title": "(2020) A.
