"https://www.academia.edu/43416584/_2020_A_G_Vlachopoulos_The_Ring_of_Nestor_and_the_quest_for_authenticity_in_F_Blakolmer_ed_Curren
t_Approaches_and_New_Perspectives_in_Aegean_Iconography_Aegis_18_2020_pp_223_252", "source_type": "paper", "published_at": null}]}, 
{"id": "20260715174913411842_f304098a", "type": "Claim", "text": "According to the recent study, the scorpion motif on the Ring of 
Nestor plays a crucial role in the overall pictorial narrative, symbolically ‘killing’ the so‑called ‘Minoan dragon’ and thereby 
providing what the author considers a coherent explanation of the ring’s complex iconography.", "source_ids": 
["20260715174845023769_648c270f"], "citations": [17], "sources": [{"source_id": "20260715174845023769_648c270f", "title": "(2020) A.
G. Vlachopoulos, “The Ring of Nestor and the quest for authenticity”, in F. Blakolmer (ed.) Current Approaches and New Perspectives 
in Aegean Iconography, Aegis 18 (2020), pp. 223-252.", "url": 
"https://www.academia.edu/43416584/_2020_A_G_Vlachopoulos_The_Ring_of_Nestor_and_the_quest_for_authenticity_in_F_Blakolmer_ed_Curren
t_Approaches_and_New_Perspectives_in_Aegean_Iconography_Aegis_18_2020_pp_223_252", "source_type": "paper", "published_at": null}]}, 
{"id": "20260715174913435911_cd17cbc0", "type": "Claim", "text": "The same recent study characterizes the Ring of Nestor’s central 
scene as one of the most populous and intricate compositions in Aegean glyptic art, centered on a ‘world tree’ whose branches host 
multiple figures and motifs.", "source_ids": ["20260715174845023769_648c270f"], "citations": [17], "sources": [{"source_id": 
"20260715174845023769_648c270f", "title": "(2020) A. G. Vlachopoulos, “The Ring of Nestor and the quest for authenticity”, in F. 
Blakolmer (ed.) Current Approaches and New Perspectives in Aegean Iconography, Aegis 18 (2020), pp. 223-252.", "url": 
"https://www.academia.edu/43416584/_2020_A_G_Vlachopoulos_The_Ring_of_Nestor_and_the_quest_for_authenticity_in_F_Blakolmer_ed_Curren
t_Approaches_and_New_Perspectives_in_Aegean_Iconography_Aegis_18_2020_pp_223_252", "source_type": "paper", "published_at": null}]}, 
{"id": "20260715174913451734_dbe3c5f0", "type": "Claim", "text": "The Ring of Nestor is described in recent scholarship as measuring
approximately 3.29 cm by 2.18 cm and as ranking among the largest known Aegean signet rings, specifically identified as the fifth 
largest in at least one comparative dataset.", "source_ids": ["20260715174845023769_648c270f"], "citations": [17], "sources": 
[{"source_id": "20260715174845023769_648c270f", "title": "(2020) A. G. Vlachopoulos, “The Ring of Nestor and the quest for 
