"https://www.academia.edu/43416584/_2020_A_G_Vlachopoulos_The_Ring_of_Nestor_and_the_quest_for_authenticity_in_F_Blakolmer_ed_Curren
t_Approaches_and_New_Perspectives_in_Aegean_Iconography_Aegis_18_2020_pp_223_252", "source_type": "paper", "published_at": null}]}, 
{"id": "20260715175934726621_451cede9", "type": "Claim", "text": "Recent scholarly work argues that the so‑called Ring of Nestor 
(CMS VI, no. 277) is an authentic Creto‑Mycenaean gold signet ring, countering earlier 1920s scholarly claims that it was a modern 
forgery and reassessing similar suspicions about other rings such as the Ring of Minos.", "source_ids": 
["20260715174845023769_648c270f"], "citations": [17], "sources": [{"source_id": "20260715174845023769_648c270f", "title": "(2020) A.
G. Vlachopoulos, “The Ring of Nestor and the quest for authenticity”, in F. Blakolmer (ed.) Current Approaches and New Perspectives 
in Aegean Iconography, Aegis 18 (2020), pp. 223-252.", "url": 
"https://www.academia.edu/43416584/_2020_A_G_Vlachopoulos_The_Ring_of_Nestor_and_the_quest_for_authenticity_in_F_Blakolmer_ed_Curren
t_Approaches_and_New_Perspectives_in_Aegean_Iconography_Aegis_18_2020_pp_223_252", "source_type": "paper", "published_at": null}]}, 
{"id": "20260715175934792749_b840044f", "type": "Claim", "text": "The reassessment of the authenticity of the Ring of Nestor and 
comparable Creto‑Mycenaean gold rings is supported by recent Late Bronze Age (16th–15th century BC) Aegean finds with related 
iconographic themes—such as wall paintings, gold rings, figurines, and ivories—and by detailed study of the techniques and 
craftsmanship of early Late Bronze Age signet rings.", "source_ids": ["20260715174845023769_648c270f"], "citations": [17], 
"sources": [{"source_id": "20260715174845023769_648c270f", "title": "(2020) A. G. Vlachopoulos, “The Ring of Nestor and the quest 
for authenticity”, in F. Blakolmer (ed.) Current Approaches and New Perspectives in Aegean Iconography, Aegis 18 (2020), pp. 
223-252.", "url": 
"https://www.academia.edu/43416584/_2020_A_G_Vlachopoulos_The_Ring_of_Nestor_and_the_quest_for_authenticity_in_F_Blakolmer_ed_Curren
t_Approaches_and_New_Perspectives_in_Aegean_Iconography_Aegis_18_2020_pp_223_252", "source_type": "paper", "published_at": null}]}, 
{"id": "20260715175934820718_fd961018", "type": "Claim", "text": "In recent scholarship, the central zoomorphic figure on the Ring 
of Nestor, previously described by Arthur Evans as a ‘watch‑dog’ or ‘dragon’ guarding an old ‘tree of the world’ whose branches 
carry one of the most populous scenes in Aegean glyptic art, is reinterpreted as a scorpion that functions as a major apotropaic 
(protective) symbol in Bronze Age Aegean iconography.", "source_ids": ["20260715174845023769_648c270f"], "citations": [17], 
"sources": [{"source_id": "20260715174845023769_648c270f", "title": "(2020) A. G. Vlachopoulos, “The Ring of Nestor and the quest 
for authenticity”, in F. Blakolmer (ed.) Current Approaches and New Perspectives in Aegean Iconography, Aegis 18 (2020), pp. 
223-252.", "url": 
"https://www.academia.edu/43416584/_2020_A_G_Vlachopoulos_The_Ring_of_Nestor_and_the_quest_for_authenticity_in_F_Blakolmer_ed_Curren
t_Approaches_and_New_Perspectives_in_Aegean_Iconography_Aegis_18_2020_pp_223_252", "source_type": "paper", "published_at": null}]}, 
{"id": "20260715175934860487_75edf5de", "type": "Claim", "text": "Within this reinterpretation, the scorpion on the Ring of Nestor 
is said to ‘kill’ the so‑called ‘Minoan dragon’ of the ring, providing a coherent narrative reading of the ring’s imagery in which 
the scorpion’s protective, apotropaic character is central to the overall iconography.", "source_ids": 
["20260715174845023769_648c270f"], "citations": [17], "sources": [{"source_id": "20260715174845023769_648c270f", "title": "(2020) A.
G. Vlachopoulos, “The Ring of Nestor and the quest for authenticity”, in F. Blakolmer (ed.) Current Approaches and New Perspectives 
in Aegean Iconography, Aegis 18 (2020), pp. 223-252.", "url": 
"https://www.academia.edu/43416584/_2020_A_G_Vlachopoulos_The_Ring_of_Nestor_and_the_quest_for_authenticity_in_F_Blakolmer_ed_Curren
t_Approaches_and_New_Perspectives_in_Aegean_Iconography_Aegis_18_2020_pp_223_252", "source_type": "paper", "published_at": null}]}, 
{"id": "20260715175935090110_b522cc9a", "type": "Claim", "text": "A longstanding scholarly tendency to treat certain Creto‑Mycenaean
gold rings, including the Ring of Nestor and the Ring of Minos, as forgeries—partly because of obscure or ‘legendary’ find 
circumstances—is explicitly critiqued in recent work, which argues that these rings have now been completely reassessed in favor of 
their authenticity.", "source_ids": ["20260715174845023769_648c270f"], "citations": [17], "sources": [{"source_id": 
"20260715174845023769_648c270f", "title": "(2020) A. G. Vlachopoulos, “The Ring of Nestor and the quest for authenticity”, in F. 
Blakolmer (ed.) Current Approaches and New Perspectives in Aegean Iconography, Aegis 18 (2020), pp. 223-252.", "url": 
"https://www.academia.edu/43416584/_2020_A_G_Vlachopoulos_The_Ring_of_Nestor_and_the_quest_for_authenticity_in_F_Blakolmer_ed_Curren
t_Approaches_and_New_Perspectives_in_Aegean_Iconography_Aegis_18_2020_pp_223_252", "source_type": "paper", "published_at": null}]}, 
{"id": "20260715175935115143_036384ea", "type": "Claim", "text": "One recent paper explicitly states that its aim is to document the
authenticity of the Ring of Nestor (CMS VI, no. 277) through both documentary and material evidence and to correct historical 
misunderstandings surrounding the ring.", "source_ids": ["20260715174845023769_648c270f"], "citations": [17], "sources": 
