analysis of the iconography surrounding the 'Ring of Nestor' in the context of Aegean forgeries and authenticity debates. By 
revisiting key iconographic features and comparisons, the paper aims to contribute to the ongoing discourse regarding the ring's 
significance in Minoan and Mycenaean art. Observations draw upon historical scholarship and recent discoveries to question and 
affirm previous conclusions related to the ring's motifs and their implications.”", "source_ids": ["20260715174314422404_df622ece"],
"citations": [14], "sources": [{"source_id": "20260715174314422404_df622ece", "title": "(PDF) SOME OBSERVATIONS ON THE ICONOGRAPHY 
