"source_type": "paper", "published_at": null}]}, {"id": "20260715174315068455_611ac5f8", "type": "Evidence", "text": "“1. The text 
explores the authenticity of the 'Ring of Nestor' through iconographic analysis.\n2. Contradictions in technical analysis highlight 
the importance of iconography in Aegean studies.\n3. The connection between incurved altars and the ring's depiction supports its 
authenticity.\n4. The ring's iconography may reflect cultural practices from the 1920s.\n5. Generations of scholars have debated the
genuineness of both Nestor's and Minos' rings.”", "source_ids": ["20260715174314422404_df622ece"], "citations": [14], "sources": 
