null}]}, {"id": "20260715175720168967_014550bb", "type": "Evidence", "text": "“Gamble, Winkelmann and Fox’s interdisciplinary study 
highlights the likely connection between the artistic rendering of the genetic anomaly and actual individuals with supernumerary 
digits, contributes to the interdisciplinary study of deformity in the prehistoric Mediterranean, and adds an interesting regional 
case study to the growing corpus of polydactylism in prehistoric societies worldwide.”", "source_ids": 
["20260715175719070732_5fed65d8"], "citations": [21], "sources": [{"source_id": "20260715175719070732_5fed65d8", "title": "[PDF] A 
Gold Signet Ring (CMS I 16) of the Aegean Late Bronze Age in it", "url": 
"https://archaeopresspublishing.com/ojs/index.php/JGA/article/download/542/210/7244", "source_type": "paper", "published_at": 
null}]}, {"id": "20260715175720181926_3e9d0a3b", "type": "Evidence", "text": "“As in other prehistoric communities, such figurines 
convey diverse meanings and functions – in the case of the Cypriot ones from dwelling–based cult figurines to sex–neutral status 
symbols, while deformity must have been viewed in a positive light within the Cypriot Chalcolithic community, ‘possibly bestowed 
upon the fortunate or divinely chosen’ (p. 8).”", "source_ids": ["20260715175719070732_5fed65d8"], "citations": [21], "sources": 
[{"source_id": "20260715175719070732_5fed65d8", "title": "[PDF] A Gold Signet Ring (CMS I 16) of the Aegean Late Bronze Age in it", 
"url": "https://archaeopresspublishing.com/ojs/index.php/JGA/article/download/542/210/7244", "source_type": "paper", "published_at":
null}]}, {"id": "20260715175720194980_c2582c45", "type": "Evidence", "text": "“Although ‘in the Cyclades, the figurines and perhaps 
the human body constituted a blank canvas onto which people not only wrote, but could also erase and rewrite or add new symbols, and
this way express, negotiate or change messages concerning to identity and status’ (p. 13), such ‘active’ palimpsests were not 
adopted in other areas (Crete and mainland southern Greece), where Cycladic–style figurines also appear.”", "source_ids": 
["20260715175719070732_5fed65d8"], "citations": [21], "sources": [{"source_id": "20260715175719070732_5fed65d8", "title": "[PDF] A 
