"https://archaeopresspublishing.com/ojs/index.php/JGA/article/download/542/210/7244", "source_type": "paper", "published_at": 
null}]}, {"id": "20260715175720208063_bdd2d356", "type": "Evidence", "text": "“Bolger’s paper identifies a shift from a fluid, 
fractal (or dividual) self (reflected in the manufacture, use, fragmentation and termination of female figurines and pendants 
associated with lifecycle rituals) to a ‘standardised self’ displayed by new forms of personal ornamentation, inspired by 
intensified cultural interactions between local Cypriot communities and those of the surrounding mainland in the 3rd millennium 
