[tools:e3d2aedd-762c-9295-2be1-ba9fddf69fd1] [AIMessage → tool] submit_final_report({'title': 'Ring of Nestor', 'sections': 
[{'title': 'Overview and Significance', 'section_type': 'lead', 'content': 'The Ring of Nestor is a gold signet ring attributed to 
the Late Bronze Age Aegean world and catalogued in the Corpus der Minoischen und Mykenischen Siegel (CMS) as CMS VI no. 
277.[15][17][20] It is widely discussed as a Creto–Mycenaean object whose engraved imagery and manufacturing techniques align with 
known Minoan and Mycenaean glyptic traditions of the 16th–15th centuries BC.[15][17][19] Recent scholarship treats the ring as an 
authentic Late Bronze Age gold signet rather than a modern forgery, situating it among the largest and most complex pictorial 
compositions known in Aegean glyptic art.[15][17]\n\nThe ring’s significance lies principally in three areas. First, its large size 
and high-quality craftsmanship place it within an elite repertoire of gold signet rings that were closely associated with status and
ritual practice in the early Mycenaean period, alongside other rich grave assemblages such as the Griffin Warrior tomb at Pylos, 
which contained four gold signet rings with Minoan ritual scenes.[1][7][10][22] Second, its complex iconography, organized around a 
"tree of the world" and a guardian creature now interpreted as a scorpion, is used to explore themes of protection, cosmology, and 
ritual in Aegean religion.[15][17][14] Third, the object has become central to debates about authenticity and forgery in Aegean 
archaeology, prompting detailed reassessment of earlier 20th‑century suspicions and contributing to broader discussions about 
Minoan–Mycenaean interaction and the transmission of religious imagery.[15][17][19]', 'source_ids': 
['20260715174314431086_1e91a4c4', '20260715174845023769_648c270f', '20260715175719060201_cfd2e8c2', '20260715175636168110_c46a0b7d',
'20260715172620525949_8d9445d4', '20260715173231956545_050c1b95', '20260715173231991407_11ba5c17', '20260715175719083632_2a1929df'],
